window.products.push({"id":131319,"name":"Jacent Fill N Brew Disposable #2 Coffee Filters, Cone Shape - 100 Count per Pack, 1 Pack","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":6.99,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/711KZwec9KS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"A good coffee filter is important for a great cup of coffee. Not every filter is equal. These disposable coffee filters not only create a delicious, richer cup of coffee ,they also will not fall apart when you remove them from the coffee maker. It is early morning and you have your cup of coffee and need to rush off to work only to return home and realize you left the filter in the coffee maker. Well no worries, just lift it out and throw it away, no reusable basket to clean. Great for the environment, easy to use and no mess cleanup!","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/711KZwec9KS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Jacent","source_asin":"B07Z4999N2","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-131319","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07Z4999N2","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07Z4999N2","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
window.products.push({"id":131320,"name":"WP3387134 3387134 Dryer Thermostat Whirlpool Kenmore Roper FSP Cycling Operating High-limit Part NED4600YQ1 NED4655EW1 NED4600YQ0 WED4815EW1 MEDC215EW","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":6.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71j9f4AgdyS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Thermostat Wp3387134 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers 3387134, AP6008270, 3387134, 2011, 2893, 3-6910, 306910, 3387135, 3387139, ET187, PS11741405, WP3387134VP. Cycling Thermostat Wp3387134 is compatible with Whirlpool, Admiral, Amana, Crosley, Estate, Inglis, Jenn-Air, Kenmore, KitchenAid, Magic Chef, Maytag, Roper. Wp3387134 Cycling Thermostat is a safety device that monitors and controls the dryer's temperature to prevent overheating and potential fire hazards. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Kenmore Dryer Part 3387134 will help if your appliance produces not enough heat, it takes too long to dry, doesn't start, or timer doesn't advance. If the thermostat fails, it can cause the dryer to overheat and result in damage or fire. Replace it as soon as possible for safe dryer operation. 💡 Whirlpool Wp3387134 is designed to be a safety device and will shut off the dryer if the temperature exceeds a certain threshold. If the temperature in the dryer exceeds this threshold, Whirlpool Thermostat 3387134 will open, interrupting the electrical circuit to the heating element, causing it to turn off. Dryer Operating Thermostat Part 3387134 meets or exceed all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 Can I bypass high limit thermostat? It is not recommended to bypass the high limit thermostat in your appliance as it is an important safety feature. 3387134 High-limit Thermostat is designed to cut off the power to the heating element if the dryer gets too hot, which helps to prevent overheating and potential fire hazards. Bypassing the high limit thermostat can cause the dryer to overheat and result in damage to the dryer or even a fire. 💡How do you check a high limit thermostat continuity? To check the continuity of a 3387134 Whirlpool Dryer Thermostat Replacement, you will need a multimeter. The steps include: disconnecting the dryer, locating the thermostat, removing the wires, setting the multimeter, and touching the leads to the terminals. A reading of zero or near-zero ohms indicates proper function, while an infinite or high resistance reading means replacement is necessary.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71j9f4AgdyS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B098XHYJCV","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-131320","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B098XHYJCV","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B098XHYJCV","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
