window.products.push({"id":131726,"name":"WP3390719 Thermal Fuse 3390719 Whirlpool Kenmore Maytag Dryer Part AP6008309 PS11741444 Replacement 110.68062801 110.62942100 110.60902990 GEW9200LW0 ","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":5.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51MwdiC3M3S._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Kenmore Dryer Thermal Fuse 3390719 - A high-quality equivalent for WP3390719, AP6008309, 15-198, 279650, 2923, 3389639, 3389640, 660877, 688841, 690198, 690798, 80004, ET402, PS11741444, WP3390719VP. Thermal Fuse Wp3390719 is compatible with Whirlpool, Kenmore, KitchenAid, Maytag. Fuse is a replacement part that is made of premium materials to ensure the durability and reliability of the dryer. Whirlpool Dryer Thermal Fuse Wp3390719 fits hundreds of models and can be installed in minutes. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace Kenmore Thermal Fuse 3390719? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Dryer Parts Wp3390719 will help if your appliance does not start, there's no heat or not enough heat, it shuts off too soon, or takes too long to dry. It is important to note that if the dryer's thermal fuse is faulty or damaged, it must be replaced immediately. 💡 Kenmore Wp3390719 is a crucial component of a dryer's safety system, designed to prevent overheating and potential fire hazards. The thermal fuse is a small, rectangular device that is typically located on the dryer's blower housing or exhaust duct. It is responsible for cutting off the dryer's power if it detects that the temperature inside the dryer is too high. 3390719 Fuse meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 How do I know if my dryer thermal fuse is blown? If your dryer thermal fuse is blown, your dryer will not start or may stop working mid-cycle. Additionally, if your dryer runs but does not produce any heat, this could also indicate that the thermal fuse has blown. To confirm whether the thermal fuse is the issue, you can use a multimeter to test the continuity of the fuse. 💡 Are all dryer thermal fuses the same? No, not all dryer thermal fuses are the same. While they may serve a similar purpose in a dryer's safety system, they are designed to operate at different temperatures and may have different physical dimensions and electrical ratings. When replacing a thermal fuse in your dryer, it is important to use the correct replacement part specified for your particular model.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51MwdiC3M3S._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07J2Z4QXQ","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-131726","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07J2Z4QXQ","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07J2Z4QXQ","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
